I ran a formal response that could be accesed through my poster and social media, of that 60% of voters said yes to paying to shut down the coal plant,
20% said no and another 20% said yes as long as we could assure that the money spent didnt go back into polluting the planet.
I also ran a more informal poll on Fizz, a University of Rochester exclusive social media, of this only 25% of people said no to paying the owners, while the other 75% said yes.
I though this was super interesting, I would have assumed that people would be more opposed to giving coal plant owners taxpayer money.


